what the shelf does now
  all kinds     outline(kind): codes[kind] ? defs() : sections(), then part()
                makes details > summary(textContent title) > div of held items
  keys          keyed(view): every details in the view, less hidden() ones
                (page.html: only details[id] under main)
  id            none. The hash is the file; a section has no address
  heading       a string. python's is decorators + the whole signature, wrapped
  edge          none
  body          lines as <pre> text blocks. md is not rendered, it is text
  look          .outline css: ring bullet, guide line, one summary style
  python        indent scan: codes.py regexes, continued(), spoken() for string
                state. No ast, and none is wanted: it is a browser file

does markdown change the same way: yes
  One function, part(), builds every kind, so the change is made once there.
  The kinds differ only in what fills heading, edge and body:

  kind     heading                          edge                 body
  md       the heading text                 sub-sections, lines  lines, as now
  py       @deco class N(b) / def n(params) glyph, size          source, marked
  js, css  signature / selector             lines                lines
  diff     path                             M  +n  -m            hunks
  hunk     the @@ line                      lines                lines
  leaf     the bare line                    lines                lines

  Nothing in md needs a rail or a glyph. It takes the node, the id and the
  edge, and keeps its body.

decided
  node       page.html's, frozen. The checker is the oracle.
  python row the def line itself, no pill: `@property def parts()`,
             `@dataclass class Field`, `class JivaRequest(Base)`. def is
             faint and means a plain method; a class says class once, as a
             card. self and cls dropped; a default over 10 chars is =...
             Hover: the full signature and the docstring. The docstring line
             is not a row. Kind is a word in the code, not a pill and not a
             glyph column.
  edge       skyline glyph (one bar per line, height the indent, 90x16) and the
             size. Nothing else, no bars.
  body       opens at the first statement. The def line and docstring are the
             row and its hover, so nothing is said twice. Comments right above
             the first statement stay.
  rail       beside the body, aligned to the lines: a bar down each if / loop
             / try / with from its head to its last line, a tick at each
             elif / else / except / finally, an arc at a loop, a blue triangle
             at return, a red cross at raise, a grey dash at break / continue.
  strings    quiet: string literals faint, comments italic and faint. Keywords
             if elif else for while try except finally with return raise break
             continue yield bold and tinted.
  folds      `. 14 fields name name ...` (an annotated name in a record's
             class body) and `. 1 small name` (defs of 3 lines or less): a
             group node, closed, its body plain lines, not nodes.
             j/k skip them.
  ids        qualified name: Field.broken_constraint

not taken, and why
  structogram, skeleton, exits table   hide code the reader wants whole
  treemap, call graph, matrix, arcs,   a second structure beside the outline;
  scatter, data cards, class cards     good as a separate view, not the outline
  signature as heading                 the how fills the line, the what is lost
  pill on every row, glyph column      noise; no mark is the default
  d3, dagre, mermaid, graphviz         shelf is one file; none was needed
  Prior art, for the record: Code::Blocks NassiShneiderman and create-struktex
  draw structograms from c and java; CodeVisualizer and Function Graph Overview
  draw a flowchart per function; none draws the code with a rail. Shneiderman's
  1982 experiments found data structure info helped more than control flow.

order
  1  node contract, md only. ids on details; keyed() takes details[id]; heading
     = first child; edge slot; body in a div; the page.html look from nesting.
     Smallest step, every kind rides it. Shelf's checker stays green, and an
     md file's keys behave as page/run.mjs says.
  2  node shape {id, heading, edge[], body} in sections() and defs(); part()
     builds from it. Diff takes its edge (M +n -m) here.
  3  python heading: kind, name, params, from the signature lines defs()
     already joins; drop self/cls, shorten defaults.
  4  python edge: the skyline from indent per line.
  5  python folds: record fields and small defs as group nodes.
  6  python body: first statement, line numbers, quiet strings, then the rail.
     4 to 6 moved to medium/page/py: a page of its own, made from the ast as
     page/diff is. The shelf does not call it yet.
  7  retire the ring and guide css for python.

the rail without an ast (the hard part)
  The picture used ast. The shelf has indent. A head is a line starting if,
  elif, else, for, while, try, except, finally, with, async for / with, ending
  in a colon at depth 0 (continued() already says a line continues). Its rail
  runs to the last non-blank line before the next line at its indent or less;
  elif, else, except, finally at the head's indent are ticks of that head's
  rail, not new ones. return, raise, break, continue by first word. Strings:
  one regex pass for ' " ''' """ with prefixes (f r b u, any case), tracking
  a triple-quoted string across lines (spoken() does this for outline).
  Compare it with oracle.py; any disagreement is a bug in one of them.

